Is there any way `H.actions` could be made user-accessible? I'd like to make an action to mark and then move down, which should be as simple as:

~~~lua
require("mini.pick").setup({
  mappings = {
    mark = nil,
    mark_and_move = {
      char = "<C-X>",
      func = function(picker)
        H.actions.mark(picker)
        H.actions.move_down(picker)
      end
    }
  }
})
~~~

but isn't because of the way actions are defined, unless I'm missing something.

> Is there any way `H.actions` could be made user-accessible? I'd like to make an action to mark and then move down,

Yeah, I thought about that. The main reason for not exporting this is that there are already too much exported and I would like to limit it.

The solution for this case I assumed would be to create custom mapping emulating "mark" and "move_down" key presses. Something like this:

```lua
require('mini.pick').setup({
  mappings = {
    mark_and_down = {
      char = '<C-d>',
      func = function() vim.api.nvim_input(vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes('<C-x><C-n>', true, true, true)) end,
    },
  },
})
```

> Do we have the option to sort the buffer list by last used?

@JSteitz I think there might still be some weird edge cases lingering, but I [ported telescope's `sort_lastused` option into MiniPick in my dotfiles](https://github.com/oncomouse/dotfiles/blob/37de1293d98ed4cc5162e7bdd182ddef91cc7955/conf/vim/lua/dotfiles/plugins/mini-nvim.lua#L448-L499).

You can use `:Pick buffers sort_lastused=true` to activate it.

> `:buffers` has a flag to get all buffers already sorted by last used. So I'm just using that. Everything else is the same, as the `builtin.buffers`. @echasnovski is this solution good and simple enough to include?

@JSteitz, I've looked into this and `:buffers t` indeed doesn't always give an up to date results. I think this is mostly because "last used" is not really well defined anywhere. For example, ibhagwan/fzf-lua also [ended up making custom solution](https://github.com/ibhagwan/fzf-lua/blob/04e7382528f3f4970cb1cd559d06ae6f7b44560e/lua/fzf-lua/providers/buffers.lua#L88-L108).

As there is a planned alternative module with a similar functionality (but for files in general), I think `sort_lastused` for buffer won't be part of `builtin.buffers()`.
